raye-update (1.0~beta2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * PCs on the Raye kernel get its new versions with the other updates;
    older kernels are removed, the newest two kept.
  * An update always ends on the newest version: a version that came out
    after the check, during the download, or while the update waited for
    the next start replaces the one that was waiting, and an older file is
    never installed in its place. The lists are read again right before an
    install, before a restart, and as the PC shuts down.
  * Raye's packages built together still wait together when only part of
    their newest version could be downloaded, also at start-up.
  * An update waiting for the restart is set again as the PC stops when
    PackageKit took it away after a look at the lists: it installs instead
    of the PC starting normally with nothing installed.
  * Check for updates always gives an answer: a check already running is
    joined, and while another install holds the package manager (the first
    start of a new system) the check waits for it, still saying Checking,
    instead of waiting six hours for the next one. The folder Settings
    watches is there from the install on.
  * The update at start-up says when a step takes a few minutes (the new
    version of the system being prepared), and on a PC that starts without
    the boot screen it shows its progress in plain text instead of a black
    screen.
  * Synaptic, which the 1.0 Beta image brought, is removed with the update;
    a copy you installed yourself stays.

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000

raye-update (1.0~beta1.1) resolute; urgency=high

  * Raye's packages that are built together now update together: an
    install while the PC is in use no longer takes part of them and leaves
    the rest for the restart. On the way from 0.5 to 1.0 Beta it took the
    new desktop without its system package, and after a plain restart the
    sign-in screen did not come up.
  * A PC an earlier update left that way finishes the update at its next
    start, whatever start that is.

