raye-update (1.0~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Updates Ubuntu hands out in phases (Plasma point releases) come in once
    everyone gets them, in one set, instead of a few packages a day.
  * A file that fails to download or turns up missing no longer stops the
    other updates or shows an error: it is tried again at the next check.
  * Raye Update says how far the check got, the download speed and time
    left, and where each update is while they install.
  * The GRUB theme, the Raye account and the admin prompt update without a
    restart.

