raye-update (0.5~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Tell about a restart again when the same packages come in newer
    versions.
  * Suspend the TPM binding before secureboot-db writes the dbx at
    start-up.
  * Restart now arms the updates even while others install in use.
  * A failed install in use waits for the restart instead of retrying
    every 6 hours.
  * Install now on a low battery says why it waits.
  * raye-shell, raye-style, raye-polkit-agent and the Plasma, KWin and
    Qt libraries wait for the restart; packages are classified by source
    too.
  * Each simulation and install in use gets its own apt pins file.
  * Finish an interrupted dpkg before asking apt anything.
  * Standard users are asked for a password every time.
  * Clear "Installing updates" when the install in use is killed.
  * The notification says "Restart now to install", since only that
    button installs the updates.
  * The 0.3 update removes WineHQ's packages once raye-wine is in, and
    nothing else.
  * The restart notice no longer gets lost when the install writes its
    state many times in a row.
  * When the 0.3 release downloaded the update, the WineHQ swap happens
    at the next check instead of never.
  * Updating from 0.3 shows "Updates are ready" too: the old notify
    watch is reloaded and started again.

